WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.644
A site has a default time zone and a default culture, but the

00:00:04.644 --> 00:00:07.799
people who use it do not all work in the same place.

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:11.551
In this video, we give a user a personal time zone and culture,

00:00:11.551 --> 00:00:13.020
and see what changes.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:22.101
By default, everyone sees dates and times in the site's time zone, and

00:00:22.101 --> 00:00:25.462
the site decides how dates and numbers are written.

00:00:25.462 --> 00:00:30.120
An editor in Paris, on a site set to Los Angeles, reads Los Angeles time.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:35.022
The User Time Zone and User Localization features add a time zone and

00:00:35.022 --> 00:00:36.628
a culture to each user.

00:00:36.628 --> 00:00:40.337
A user who picks them sees dates and times in that time zone,

00:00:40.337 --> 00:00:44.600
written in that culture, while everyone else keeps the site's settings.

00:00:48.768 --> 00:00:53.549
Here is a blog post on the site, which uses the Los Angeles time zone.

00:00:53.549 --> 00:00:57.826
The header says it was posted on March 14, 2026, and the month

00:00:57.826 --> 00:00:59.588
is written in English.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.815
To change that, let's enable two features.

00:01:02.815 --> 00:01:07.364
Under Tools, Features, a search for User Time Zone finds the feature that

00:01:07.364 --> 00:01:09.841
adds a time zone field to every user.

00:01:09.841 --> 00:01:11.280
Enable turns it on.

00:01:11.758 --> 00:01:15.651
Next, we enable User Localization, which adds a culture field.

00:01:15.651 --> 00:01:20.746
It depends on the Localization feature, listed beside it, which keeps the supported

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:23.208
cultures and is enabled on this site.

00:01:23.674 --> 00:01:29.364
Under Settings, Localization, Cultures, a table lists the cultures the site supports, and

00:01:29.364 --> 00:01:31.341
one of them is the default.

00:01:31.341 --> 00:01:33.677
The Add culture button adds more.

00:01:33.677 --> 00:01:36.134
A user can only choose among these.

00:01:40.335 --> 00:01:44.228
In Access Control, Users, every account has an Edit button.

00:01:44.228 --> 00:01:48.839
Let's edit the administrator, the account we are signed in with, so the

00:01:48.839 --> 00:01:51.115
result is visible straight away.

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:53.959
Further down the page are two fields:

00:01:53.959 --> 00:01:56.673
Default Time Zone and Default User Culture.

00:01:56.673 --> 00:02:00.549
Both start on the option that leaves the choice to the site, Use

00:02:00.549 --> 00:02:03.097
site's time zone and Use site's culture.

00:02:03.561 --> 00:02:07.599
Default Time Zone lists time zones, each with its offset and name.

00:02:07.599 --> 00:02:13.040
Its hint says it determines the time zone used when displaying and editing dates and times.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:14.891
Let's choose Europe, Paris.

00:02:15.346 --> 00:02:19.116
Default User Culture offers the cultures the site supports.

00:02:19.116 --> 00:02:21.553
Let's choose French and select Save.

00:02:21.553 --> 00:02:26.019
A message confirms the update, and because this is our own account, the

00:02:26.019 --> 00:02:27.876
change applies right away.

00:02:32.061 --> 00:02:37.373
Back on the blog post, the header shows the 15th, with the month written in French.

00:02:37.373 --> 00:02:41.491
The post was created in the evening of the 14th in Los Angeles,

00:02:41.491 --> 00:02:45.191
which is already the early morning of the 15th in Paris.

00:02:49.391 --> 00:02:52.495
For the time zone, the user's choice comes first.

00:02:52.495 --> 00:02:56.219
If it is left on Use site's time zone, the Default Time Zone

00:02:56.219 --> 00:03:01.411
in Settings, General applies, where Local to server means the time zone of the server.

00:03:02.161 --> 00:03:06.302
For the culture, a personal choice applies to that user's pages, and only

00:03:06.302 --> 00:03:08.871
the cultures the site supports are offered.

00:03:08.871 --> 00:03:12.646
Use site's culture leaves the choice to the site, as for a visitor

00:03:12.646 --> 00:03:14.061
who is not signed in.

00:03:14.811 --> 00:03:19.948
An administrator sets these fields for any user from Access Control, Users, Edit.

00:03:19.948 --> 00:03:24.791
A user with the Edit own user information and Access admin panel permissions

00:03:24.791 --> 00:03:27.684
reaches them from Profile in the user menu.

00:03:27.684 --> 00:03:30.991
Visitors who are not signed in are never affected.

00:03:32.991 --> 00:03:37.214
That is how User Time Zone and User Localization give each user a

00:03:37.214 --> 00:03:39.415
personal time zone and culture.

00:03:39.415 --> 00:03:40.961
Thanks for watching.

